    "eventMetadata": {
     "context_description": "Xi Jinping\u2019s entrenched authority within the Chinese Communist Party and People\u2019s Liberation Army underpins the 95.5% trader consensus against his removal before 2027. Recent military purges, including the January 2026 sidelining of senior generals, have eliminated potential rivals and reinforced loyalty rather than signaling weakness, while preparations for the 21st Party Congress point toward expectations of a fourth term. No major leadership challenges or health developments have surfaced in the past several months to shift this assessment. The wisdom of crowds reflected in current pricing accounts for the opacity of elite politics and historical patterns of incumbent consolidation in one-party systems. Sudden health events, severe economic shocks prompting elite realignment, or unforeseen external crises remain low-probability factors that could still alter outcomes within the resolution window.",
     "context_requires_regen": false,
